# mcp-coder (strict)

## Planner vs executor

| Phase | You (Cursor) | MCP / Aider |
|-------|----------------|-------------|
| **Epic** | `specs/epics/<slug>.md` | — |
| **Step task** | `specs/tasks/<epic>-<step>.md` (one file per step; keep for audit) | — |
| **Review** (optional) | `delegate_to_agent(mode=review, spec_path=…, target_files=[], task=…)` | Questions → report **Worker feedback** |
| **Refine** | Update **same** task spec (`revision++`, `status: ready`); human input if needed | — |
| **Implement** | `delegate_to_agent(mode=implement, spec_path=…, target_files=[edit + read deps], …)` | Edits code; report Run log |

- **Never** implement on disk yourself.
- **Never** delegate planning (writing epic/step specs).
- **Do not** use implement mode to brainstorm — use **review** or Cursor chat.
- **Do not** edit `specs/reports/` (MCP-owned).
- After implement: follow **workspace-history** rule (MCP inspect tools + local tests); then set task `status: done` + checkboxes; update epic Steps table.

After each `delegate_to_agent` call: summarize `success`, `outcome`, `delegate_mode`, `delegation_id`, `spec_report_path`, `files_changed`, `files_unexpected`.

## Read-deps (implement mode)

`target_files` must include **every** path Aider needs in context — not only files to edit:

- **Edit** — files the step will change.
- **Read** — prior-step outputs, imports, types, or APIs the worker must see (Aider loads full file text).
- List both in the task spec **Files** section (`### Edit` / `### Read`); pass **all** paths in `target_files`.
- Step N+1 implement: include step N deliverables in read-deps (e.g. module created in step 1).
- `mode=review` does **not** replace read-deps on implement — review is spec-only (`target_files=[]`).

